/E (At the turn of the millennium, WorldCom stood as a titan of the American telecommunications industry. However, behind its rapid growth lay a fragile foundation. By 2002, the company was already struggling under a staggering $41 billion debt. All while the corporate world was still reeling from the recent Enron collapse.)
